DTSTAMP:20260804T033345Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53550588366804
DTSTART:20270113T150000Z
DTEND:20270113T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the African American Cultural Center to experience ariana 
 Farquharson's You Are Here: Geolocating the Self through the Familiar in t
 he Midst of the Unfamiliar. The exhibition is a speculative\, immersive wo
 rld-building study that invites guests to explore (geo)locating self and h
 ome amid a rapidly and frequently changing post-pandemic “new” world. 
 It will be on display in the art gallery at the African American Cultural 
 Center from Oct. 28\, 2026\, to  Feb. 28\, 2027. A behind-the-scenes look 
 at the exhibition is set for Nov. 11.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center (218
 )
SUMMARY:You Are Here Exhibition
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/you-are-here-geolocating-the-
 self-through-the-familiar-in-the-midst-of-the-unfamiliar-exhibition
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
