BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20260804T033345Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53496551412437
DTSTART:20270128T223000Z
DTEND:20270129T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the African American Cultural Center (AACC) for the EQUIP 
 spring check-in and to learn how this year-long initiative can help you cr
 eate the college experience you want in and outside of the classroom. EQUI
 P stands for Empower\, Question\, Understand\, Initiate and Partner. The i
 nitiative is designed to help first-year students:\n\nEmpower themselves t
 o create the college experience they wantQuestion everything to build habi
 ts for life-long learningUnderstand themselves and what they need to be su
 ccessfulInitiate action and be proactive to find resourcesPartner with oth
 ers to build a network of care and communityAs an EQUIP participant\, you 
 will:\n\nEngage in monthly check-ins with a dedicated staff memberAttend l
 earning labs and AACC signature eventsWork with an embedded AACC counselor
 Attend EQUIP special programsDevelop skills in self-awareness\, resilience
  and help-seekingContact Andaiye Qaasim\, assistant director of the AACC\,
  at aaqaasim@ncsu.edu if you have questions.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center (Roo
 m 356)
SUMMARY:EQUIP Spring Check-in
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/equip-spring-check-in
CATEGORIES:Student Life
CATEGORIES:High-Impact Experiences
END:VEVENT
